the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base derogatesfrom includes these resources:
    lomo.

the templates are:
    *a party* processes personal data that a contract needs.
    *a party* makes only vehicles of the exempt categories.

the knowledge base derogatesfrom includes:

the text of the source description is at "sources/derogatesFrom.ttl".

% Who bears a duty: the agent of this role of the action (lomo.le).
the bearer role is addresser.

the texts of "skos:note" have no language.


norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_Dir2013_34_Art1_GeneralObligation".

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation is a prescriptive rule.

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation has the label "Directive 2013/34/EU Article 1(2)(a): General requirement for financial statements".

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation has the comment "All undertakings shall prepare annual financial statements".

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation has the modality obligation.

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2013/34/oj/art_1".


norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_Dir2013_34_Art1a_MicroEntityDerogation".

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity is a prescriptive rule.

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity has the label "Directive 2013/34/EU Article 1a: Derogation for micro-entities".

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity has the comment "Micro-entities are exempt from the requirements of Articles 4 to 8 and 19a".

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity has the modality permission.

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity derogates from norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation.

norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2013/34/oj/art_1a".


norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_GDPR_Art6_1_a_Consent".

norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent is a prescriptive rule.

norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent has the label "GDPR Article 6(1)(a): Lawful basis - Consent".

norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent has the comment "Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that consent has been given".

norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent has the modality permission.

norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/art_6/par_1/point_a".


norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_GDPR_Art6_1_b_ContractPerformance".

norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance is a prescriptive rule.

norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance has the label "GDPR Article 6(1)(b): Lawful basis - Contract performance".

norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance has the comment "Processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party".

norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance has the modality permission.

norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance derogates from norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent.

norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/art_6/par_1/point_b".

norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance has for "skos:note" the value "Article 6(1)(b) provides an alternative lawful basis that substitutes consent when contract performance is necessary (substitutive derogation)".


norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_EU2019_1242_Art4_CO2Monitoring".

norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring is a substantive rule.

norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring has the label "Regulation (EU) 2019/1242 Article 4: CO₂ monitoring".

norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring has the comment "Manufacturers shall monitor CO₂ emissions and fuel consumption".

norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring has the modality obligation.

norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2019/1242/art_4".


norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_EU2019_1242_Art5_4_VehicleDerogation".

norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation is a prescriptive rule.

norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation has the label "Regulation (EU) 2019/1242 Article 5(4): Derogation from monitoring for certain vehicles".

norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation has the comment "The monitoring requirements of Article 4 shall not apply to vehicles of certain categories or with specific characteristics".

norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation has the modality permission.

norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation derogates from norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring.

norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2019/1242/art_5/par_4".

norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation has for "skos:note" the value "Article 5(4) provides a blocking derogation that suspends the general monitoring obligation for specified vehicle categories".


% The questions of LOMO's requirements document (its competency questions),
% as far as a description can answer them.
scenario description is, as stated in the source description:
    modalities expects answers ["norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity has the modality permission", "norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation has the modality obligation", "norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring has the modality obligation", "norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation has the modality permission", "norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent has the modality permission", "norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance has the modality permission"].

scenario micro_entities is, as stated in the source description:
    norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation produces prepare the statements.
    prepare the statements has the agent role role preparer.
    role preparer is for the agent undertakings.
    role preparer has the role addresser.
    norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity produces use the micro regime.
    use the micro regime has the agent role role micro.
    role micro is for the agent micro entities.
    role micro has the role addresser.
    acme is of the type undertakings.
    tiny is of the type undertakings.
    tiny is of the type micro entities.
    applies expects answers ["norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation applies to acme", "norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity applies to tiny"].
    set_aside expects answers ["norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation is set aside for tiny by norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity"].
    obliged expects answers ["acme is obliged that acme performs prepare the statements"].

scenario consent_or_contract is, as stated in the source description:
    norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent produces process personal data.
    norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance produces process personal data.
    process personal data has the agent role role controller.
    role controller is for the agent controllers.
    role controller has the role addresser.
    norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance has written conditions.
    the conditions of norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance hold for a party if
        the party counts as controllers
        and the party processes personal data that a contract needs.
    shop is of the type controllers.
    shop processes personal data that a contract needs.
    club is of the type controllers.
    applies expects answers ["norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent applies to club", "norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance applies to shop"].
    set_aside expects answers ["norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent is set aside for shop by norm gdpr art 6 1 b contract performance"].
    rules_without_conditions expects answers ["norm dir 2013 34 art 1 general obligation has no written conditions", "norm dir 2013 34 art 1 a micro entity has no written conditions", "norm gdpr art 6 1 a consent has no written conditions", "norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring has no written conditions", "norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation has no written conditions"].

scenario exempt_vehicles is, as stated in the source description:
    norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring produces monitor the emissions.
    norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation produces leave the vehicles unmonitored.
    monitor the emissions has the agent role role monitor.
    leave the vehicles unmonitored has the agent role role monitor.
    role monitor is for the agent manufacturers.
    role monitor has the role addresser.
    norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation has written conditions.
    the conditions of norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation hold for a party if
        the party counts as manufacturers
        and the party makes only vehicles of the exempt categories.
    truckco is of the type manufacturers.
    busco is of the type manufacturers.
    busco makes only vehicles of the exempt categories.
    applies expects answers ["norm eu 2019 1242 art 4 co 2 monitoring applies to truckco", "norm eu 2019 1242 art 5 4 vehicle derogation applies to busco"].
    obliged expects answers ["truckco is obliged that truckco performs monitor the emissions"].
    permitted expects answers ["busco is permitted that busco performs leave the vehicles unmonitored"].

query applies is:
    which rule applies to which party.

query rules_without_conditions is:
    which rule has no written conditions.

query places is:
    which rule is laid down in which place.

query derogations is:
    which rule is a derogation from which second rule.

query kinds is:
    which thing is of the kind which kind.

query rules_of_act is:
    which rule is established by the act which act.

query provisions is:
    which thing is established in which provision.

query joint_rules is:
    which rule is established in more than one provision.

query prescriptive is:
    which thing is a prescriptive rule.

query constitutive is:
    which thing is a constitutive rule.

query modalities is:
    which rule has the modality which modality.

query set_aside is:
    which rule is set aside for which party by which second rule.

query obliged is:
    which party is obliged that which sentence.

query permitted is:
    which party is permitted that which sentence.

query forbidden is:
    which party is forbidden that which sentence.

query holders_of_rights is:
    which party has the right that which sentence.

query violations is:
    the obligation of which party that which sentence is violated.

query parts is:
    which thing is part of the description.

query texts is:
    which thing is described by the text which text.

query other_values is:
    which thing has for which property the value which value.

query addresses is:
    which thing is identified by which address.

query plain_texts is:
    the texts of which property have no language.

query bearer is:
    the bearer role is which role.

